1641:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * @param  event Receive FIFO events to be cleared. \n
1642:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 			\b Range: @ref XMC_USIC_CH_RXFIFO_EVENT_STANDARD, @ref XMC_USIC_CH_RXFIFO_EVENT_ERROR,
1643:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * 					  @ref XMC_USIC_CH_RXFIFO_EVENT_ALTERNATE.
1644:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * @return None
1645:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
1646:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * \par<b>Description</b><br>
1647:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * Clears the receive FIFO event flags in the status register. \n\n
1648:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * USIC channel peripheral does not clear the event flags after they are read.
1649:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * This API clears the events provided in the \a mask value. 
1650:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * XMC_USIC_CH_RXFIFO_EVENT enumeration can be used as input. Multiple events
1651:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * can be cleared by providing a mask value obtained by bitwise OR operation of 
1652:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  * multiple event enumerations.
1653:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_usic.h ****  *
